  "result": "Perfect! **All 346 tests pass!** The dashboard function is now complete and fully tested. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Dashboard Implementation \u2713\n\n**Added to src/reports.js:**\n\n```javascript\ndashboard(invoices, asOf) \u2192 { counts, outstanding, overdue, topCustomers }\n```\n\n**Returns:**\n- **counts**: Object with invoice counts per status (draft, issued, partially_paid, paid)\n- **outstanding**: Total amount still due on issued and partially_paid invoices\n- **overdue**: Object with { count, amount } from overdue invoices\n- **topCustomers**: 3 customers with highest outstanding amounts as [{ customerId, due }], sorted highest first\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Counts invoices by all status types\n- Aggregates outstanding amounts from issued and partially_paid invoices only\n- Includes payment-aware amounts (calls balanceDue for each invoice)\n- Identifies top customers by outstanding balance (limits to 3)\n- Leverages existing overdueInvoices() function for consistency\n- Handles edge cases: fewer than 3 customers, no outstanding invoices, zero overdue amounts\n\n**Test Coverage (11 comprehensive tests):**\n- \u2713 Counts invoices by status\n- \u2713 Calculates outstanding amount\n- \u2713 Identifies overdue invoices\n- \u2713 Handles no overdue invoices\n- \u2713 Identifies top 3 customers\n- \u2713 Handles fewer than 3 customers\n- \u2713 Handles no outstanding invoices\n- \u2713 Excludes paid invoices from outstanding\n- \u2713 Mixed invoice statuses\n- \u2713 Correct return structure\n- \u2713 Top customers sorted by amount\n\n**All Tests:** 346/346 passing \u2713\n\nThe dashboard provides a single-call view of key business metrics for invoices as of a specific date.",
